cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "SETx-1km-CMIP6: A 1 km dual-kriging downscaled NEX-GDDP-CMIP6 dataset for Eastern Texas (code)"
type: software
version: "v1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-28"
doi: "PLACEHOLDER"
license: BSD 3-Clause License
repository-code: "PLACEHOLDER-REPO-URL"
abstract: >-
  This includes codes that downscale NEX-GDDP-CMIP6 model output to 1-km daily fields over East Texas using universal kriging (KrigR), and codes that run quality control and evaluation on those fields. It covers eight variables: near-surface air temperature (tas), daily maximum and minimum temperature (tasmax, tasmin), near-surface wind speed (sfcWind), specific and relative humidity (huss, hurs), and downwelling longwave and shortwave radiation (rlds, rsds). The downscaling stage uses a gated pipeline that enforces a per-iteration coverage gate and deletes failing timesteps. Precipitation (pr) is out of scope.
keywords:
  - CMIP6
  - NEX-GDDP-CMIP6
  - statistical downscaling
  - kriging
  - KrigR
  - East Texas
  - Southeast Texas
  - quality control
  - evaluation
